think SHA-256 is the 32-bit sibling of the GREEN sha512.rye — same Merkle–Damgård shape over u32 words: eight-word init, sixty-four round constants, Ch/Maj/big/small-sigma with the SHA-256 rotation set, sixty-four rounds, 64-byte block, 0x80 marker + 64-bit big-endian bit length, the second-block edge at rem >= 56. Authored crypto/sha256.rye by mirroring the house style exactly (bounds, ≥2 contract asserts per fn, wrapping +% mod 2^32, MessageTooLong at the edge, no std.crypto in the primitive).
